  "finding": "Flat scan + IN(all READY ids) prefilter: ~2.4 us/row p50 (1.1 s at 0.5M rows, 4.7 s at 2M, 9.7 s at 4M, 19.6 s at 8M). The IN filter adds ~60-70% over an unfiltered flat scan. IVF_PQ cuts p50 to 0.1-0.5 s at 2M-8M rows with refine, but with the IN-list prefilter the cost still grows linearly with rows (filter evaluation), so ANN alone does not remove the O(N) term. SQLite eligible-id load + IN-string build are small (<0.05 s at 66k versions)."
